<section class="service-detail">
  <div class="text-content faq-block">

    <h3>Is your facility's fire protection system ready for an emergency?</h3>
    <p>
      Regular inspection and maintenance help ensure fire equipment is ready when needed. Check hydrants,
      extinguishers and other fire protection equipment for faults, damage or overdue servicing.
    </p>

    <h3>When was the last time your fire hydrants were inspected?</h3>
    <p>
      Fire hydrants should be inspected and serviced at the required intervals for your site and applicable
      standards. Regular checks can identify leaks, corrosion, damage or other problems before an emergency
      occurs.
    </p>

    <h3>What should Australian businesses know about fire safety compliance?</h3>
    <p>
      Australian businesses need to manage workplace fire risks, maintain an effective emergency plan and
      keep required fire protection equipment properly maintained. Exact requirements can vary by state,
      territory, building type and site risk.
    </p>

    <h3>How often should commercial fire extinguishers be inspected?</h3>
    <p>
      Under AS 1851 practices, portable fire extinguishers are generally serviced at six-monthly intervals,
      with additional yearly and five-yearly servicing requirements where applicable. Your site's legal and
      building requirements should also be checked.
    </p>

    <h2 class="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>What do professional fire services include?</h3>
    <p>
      Professional fire services can include fire extinguisher testing and tagging, extinguisher
      replacement, fire hydrant inspections, repairs, upgrades and ongoing maintenance.
    </p>

    <h3>Why is regular fire hydrant maintenance important?</h3>
    <p>
      Regular maintenance helps identify damage, corrosion, leaks and other faults before they affect the
      hydrant's performance. It helps keep essential fire equipment ready for an emergency.
    </p>

    <h3>When should a fire hydrant be repaired or upgraded?</h3>
    <p>
      A hydrant may need repair or upgrading when inspections find damage, leaks, corrosion, poor
      performance or ageing components. A qualified fire services professional can assess what action is
      required.
    </p>

    <h3>When should a facility engage a professional fire services provider?</h3>
    <p>
      Engage a professional provider for scheduled inspections, testing, repairs, upgrades or whenever fire
      equipment shows signs of damage or poor performance. Planned maintenance can help identify problems
      before they become urgent.
    </p>

    <h2 class="faq-heading">Talk to TWS About Fire Services</h2>
    <p>
      Need help with fire hydrants, extinguisher servicing or ongoing fire protection maintenance? Speak
      with TWS Service &amp; Solutions about a practical fire services solution for your facility.
    </p>
